message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "TROVE: a flow-labelled hardware-Trojan benchmark"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fazeli
    given-names: Mahdi
    affiliation: Halmstad University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2874-6256"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24525130"
version: "1.1-draft"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MahdiFazeli79/ht-benchmark"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - hardware Trojan
  - benchmark
  - logic synthesis
  - hardware security
abstract: >-
  A hardware-Trojan benchmark whose labels are defined per synthesis flow.
  Each sample is a Trojan inserted into an ISCAS-89 or ITC'99 host circuit,
  and each (sample, flow) pair carries a label record stating whether the
  Trojan is functional, inert or removed after synthesis, with the
  equivalence proof and the witness that support the label.
